this is El muttona B Street a landmark  in baghdad's city center  it's a cultural Hub and a space for  artists and activists to share opinions  these days the conversations are often  about Iraq's latest political  developments  we've learned from this year's incidents  that confrontation with the state is not  the only option to seek change we are  now regrouping with other political  activists to create a unified voice  based on National interest unfortunately  all unrest are prevailed through the  year was based on partisan interest it's  a conflict overpower  that conflict was between major Shia  political parties following the  elections in 2021  it led to the suspension of  parliamentary process and derailed the  formation of a new government  in June politicians affiliated with  influential Shia leader muktada quit  when rival parties backed by Iran  nominated Muhammad al-sudani as prime  minister so the supporters took the  streets  in August thousands stormy bardad's  heavily fortified green zone and  occupied the Parliament building holding  a city in that lasted weeks  the conflict peaked when crowds stormed  the presidential Palace  dozens of people were killed as they  were driven out of the compound by  Security Forces  other protests were staged through the  year  calls for political and economic reform  order was finally restored when the  Sudani government took office in October  scenes like this give the impression of  normality but the same issue is way  heavy on Iraqis after one year political  deadlock they finally have a government  but economic challenges and underlying  political rivalries both crucial to  ensuring stability  remain unresolved  and many are skeptical that anything  will change under the new Administration  every government breaks its promises  with the people life has become so  difficult unemployment is exacerbating  at all prices are getting higher  nepotism and Corruption are deeply  rooted in state institutions we have no  hope that a change will happen anytime  soon  the world food program said poverty  levels reached nearly 32 percent in 2020  even though Iraq is the second largest  producer of crude oil after Saudi Arabia  in the OPEC group of oil producing  countries  over the past three years many  development projects were aborted  because of political unrest now the  government and Parliament need to pass a  budget for the upcoming year as soon as  possible that would help mitigate  current economic difficulties because  the New Year's budget is estimated  around 200 billion dollars  in October authorities revealed billions  of dollars had been embezzled from State  funds and promised to recover the money  many Iraqis hope it is the beginning of  the end of government corruption
 

